  "CAVEATS": "v2a-dist: conv3 DOWNSTREAM (least-excited) family characterized by threshold-defined per-channel tail SUBSPACES (sigma<=tau*sigma_max of each channel's gated-mean-patch Gram, tau in TAUS), not single per-channel directions. Per tau we sample M perturbations drawing, for each channel, a random unit direction from that channel's tail subspace (random per-channel amplitude), and report the drift DISTRIBUTION (median/p5/p95) across radii, versus matched controls: a dimension-matched per-channel random subspace (randsub) and generic full-operator random directions (generic). Per-channel gated-mean-patch construction respects avgpool + relu-gate (fixed at base) + weight sharing + eval BN. The downstream family CONTAINS the feature-null by construction; empirically it is a much larger APPROXIMATE tail (no exact downstream-null: per-channel Grams full rank at N=4000, exact_null_dim_total=0, via per-channel sigma_min median). Directions validated by the local forward (cross-checked to full net in v1). conv1/conv2 downstream (through further nonlinear layers) and multilayer branches are v2b. Env: RESNET_M, RESNET_TAUS, RESNET_SEED."
